            <link>https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/cuban-official-on-trumps-threats-as-tensions-with-u-s-rise</link>
            <description><![CDATA[For months, the Trump administration has ramped up pressure and threats against Cuba. A de facto oil blockade now means hours of blackouts, plus food and water shortages for millions on the island. While President Trump has threatened a takeover, Cuban officials say they're still willing to talk. Amna Nawaz discussed the tensions with Carlos Fernández de Cossío, Cuba's deputy foreign minister.]]></description>
